A||||7||onfire||Runs good when cold, runs bad when hot. 2.5 duke.||||1||
Z||000000||onfire||08-11-2001||04:31 AM||||I am buying my 87 fiero back for $200. The guy who has it now says it runs fine until it warms up. I am going to pick the car up either sat. or sun. I will know more then. Just wanted to get some ideas going on what the problem might be.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mbramble||08-11-2001||09:12 AM||||That's the way my 87 coupe was when I inherited it.  Ran great cold, as soon as it warmed up -- backfiring, missing, stalling, etc.  It was a bad coil pack.  Obviously had a heat related problem.  Pontiac dealer replaced it and it has run great since...||||reg||1
Z||000002||onfire||08-11-2001||11:50 AM||||That's what my uncle was thinking. So it looks like I will replace that first. I just wanted a second opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-11-2001||01:59 PM||||Bad coil or crank pickup could be it. <P>MAT or ECT may also be batty.<P>None of them are hard to fix or very expencive. notes on all in my cave.<P>Could also be a fuel pump issue. Fill the gas tank and see if that effects it. A full tank keeps the pump cooler.<P><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||08-11-2001||08:43 PM||||Read the DIS article in my cave. if the shield is missing from the ignition module then the coils will over heat.||||reg||1
Z||000005||862M4inCA||08-13-2001||11:01 AM||||Might not hurt to check something as simple as the O2 sensor either. Especially if the SES/CE light is coming on. However in my case the SES/CE light didn't show ANY signs of life that there was an O2 problem, and the computer never gave any more info than a code 12. The ceramic inside the O2 sensor was litterally blown apart as you could hear it rattle around when it was removed. New O2 and it ran like a champ warm or cold. Definately a cheap test since O2 sensors are generally pretty cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000006||onfire||08-13-2001||01:50 PM||||Well I picked it up sat. night. It started up fine. Drove it to the street light, it was hesitent after it got moving at part throttle. I either had to floor it or baby it, to get it moving. It did alright on the freeway, except for the big hill we went up. It died when we got off the freeway, so we towed it the last two blocks. I checked the cave on how to replace the coil packs. Thanks theogre for all the info on the website. I haven't messed with the car yet. Its parked at a friends house. I may get it running and sell it. So I have more money for my 85 GT. Although I change my mind everyday.<BR>The maroon one is the one I bought back. Anybody want it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2ofthem.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by onfire (edited 08-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||08-13-2001||02:57 PM||||Yes, I vote for O2. It goes closed loop and the O2 is dead so it pumps up the fuel.||||reg||1
